---
description: SupportPilot conventions
alwaysApply: true
---
- Python 3.12, FastAPI, Pydantic v2, type hints everywhere.
- The LLM is NEVER called inside an HTTP request handler; publish a Kafka event instead.
- Kafka consumers: manual commits, idempotent processing, DLQ after N failures.
- Agent tools are read-only. Anything that changes money or data goes through human approval in n8n.
- Never hardcode secrets; read env vars. Secrets live in AWS Secrets Manager.
- Every new endpoint or agent behavior needs a pytest test (mock the LLM and HTTP tools).
- Event shapes live in /contracts. Change the schema first, then the code.
- Log `ticket_id` on every line touching a ticket.
